That leaves A–G. Colleague 4’s chronology point on C is well taken: Lady Saigō’s death in 1634 predates the 1676 compilation by more than four decades, so any techniques she might have used would already have been long obsolete and unlikely to drive later Toba-domain redaction. Similar temporal or institutional mismatches weaken A (Fujibayashi’s alleged pre-presentation erasure) and D (Oniwaban not formally organized until the 1710s–20s).  

